Switches one or more digital outputs (relays) on the router in response to
Cumulocity IoT operations.

This is an extension for the thin-edge.io platform Router App. It registers two
Cumulocity custom operations with the thin-edge.io mapper:

  * c8y_Relay        - a single relay (relayState OPEN/CLOSED); drives the first
                       configured output.
  * c8y_RelayArray   - the Cumulocity RelayArray widget; drives every configured
                       output from the matching array position.

The new state is reflected into the device managed object so the relay widgets
update, and the initial state is seeded on start so the widget renders one toggle
per output. It also registers its settings with Cumulocity configuration
management, so the output list can be changed from the cloud.

Works on ICR routers that expose binary outputs via the ICR-OS "io" command,
including the ICR-1642 (one output: out0) and the ICR-44xx family (out0 out1).
List the outputs this device controls in MOD_RELAY_OUTPUTS (exact `io` names,
e.g. "out0 out1", or an expansion-port name).

Install the thin-edge.io platform module first, then this extension. Enable it on
this module's configuration page. See docs/EXTENSION-API.md.
